<title>UK: ICCO details result of cocoa buffer stock sale.</title>
<headline>ICCO details result of cocoa buffer stock sale.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Cocoa Organization (ICCO) said the 4,250 tonne buffer-stock sale earlier on Monday was completed at the following prices.</p>
<p>ORIGIN	 TONNES  PORT	CROP YEAR  QUALITY  U.S.DLR/T</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire    70  Amsterdam  1979/80    GF     $1,300</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire 1,773  Amsterdam  1981/82    GF     $1,354-$1,355</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire 1,374  Amsterdam  1981/82    FF     $1,278-$1,280</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire    99  Amsterdam  1982/83    GF     $1,354</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire   556  Amsterdam  1982/83    FF     $1,280</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire   274  Amsterdam  1987/88    GF     $1,400</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire    51  Rotterdam  1987/88    FF     $1,280</p>
<p>Togo		 54  Rotterdam  1987/88    GF     $1,400</p>
<p>(GF=good fermented, FF=fair fermented)</p>
<p>The ICCO said the carry for forward delivery was calculated at $12 per tonne per month.</p>
<p>-- Clelia Oziel, London Newsroom 44 171 542 8072.</p>
</text>
